From: Li Zhe <lizhe.67@bytedance.com>
Date: Thu, 3 Sep 2026 10:58:06 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] 
 mm-add-a-template-based-fast-path-for-zone-device-page-init-fix

whitespace fix, per Mike

Link: https://lore.kernel.org/20260903025806.70825-1-lizhe.67@bytedance.com
Signed-off-by: Li Zhe <lizhe.67@bytedance.com>
Cc: Mike Rapoport (Microsoft) <rppt@kernel.org>
Signed-off-by: Andrew Morton <akpm@linux-foundation.org>
---
 mm/mm_init.c | 3 +--
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/mm/mm_init.c b/mm/mm_init.c
index be9a588b0f540..59a101a6d6909 100644
--- a/mm/mm_init.c
+++ b/mm/mm_init.c
@@ -1139,8 +1139,7 @@ void __ref memmap_init_zone_device(struct zone *zone,
 	for (; pfn < end_pfn; pfn += pfns_per_compound) {
 		page = pfn_to_page(pfn);
 
-		zone_device_page_init_from_template(page, pfn,
-						    &template);
+		zone_device_page_init_from_template(page, pfn, &template);
 
 		if (IS_ALIGNED(pfn, PAGES_PER_SECTION))
 			cond_resched();
-- 
2.47.3

